  + [implementation_language] is safe Rust edition 2024
  + [activation_state] is active_for_bounded_implementation_and_evidence

& [AuthorityBoundary] is non-waivable
  = must: preserve exact source bytes and bind every lowered unit to one verified quote
  = must: reject every unsupported, malformed, ambiguous, duplicate, or out-of-limit input before signing
  = must: use stable semantic identity independent of display path and line number
  = must: keep private key material outside source, manifest, environment, request, response, log, and receipt artifacts
  = must: preserve PackageCompiler, TrustStore, ProtocolRequest, ProtocolResponse, CLI, PreparedRuntime, and MCP semantic authority
  - never: infer semantic relationships not declared by the bounded lowering profile
  - never: claim full SOP, neural, database, service, distributed, model-state, or FPGA implementation through this slice

& [BoundedSourceGrammar] is exact
  + [metadata_subject] is exactly one unindented Subject colon followed by nonempty text
  + [metadata_description] is zero or one unindented Description colon followed by nonempty text
  + [named_subject] is ampersand, one space, bracketed nonempty name, one space, and nonempty body
  + [named_member] is plus, one space, bracketed nonempty name, one space, and nonempty body
  + [named_reference] is at sign, one space, bracketed nonempty name, one space, and nonempty body
  + [named_claim] is exclamation mark, one space, bracketed nonempty name, one space, and nonempty body
  + [directive] is equals sign, one space, and nonempty body
  + [constraint] is minus sign, one space, and nonempty body
  + [ignored] is blank lines and lines whose first nonspace byte is hash
  + [indentation] is ASCII spaces in exact two-space levels with no tab
  + [parent] is the nearest prior lowered node exactly one indentation level shallower
  + [root] is a lowered node at zero indentation
  + [encoding] is valid UTF-8
  + [line_endings] is LF or CRLF
  + [source_span] is marker through final non-line-ending byte and excludes indentation and line ending
  - never: ignore an unknown nonblank line or decode invalid UTF-8 with replacement

& [LoweringProfile] is conservative asserted meaning
  + [ampersand] is UnitKind Term
  + [plus] is UnitKind Declaration
  + [at_sign] is UnitKind Relation
  + [exclamation] is UnitKind Judgment
  + [equals] is UnitKind Operation
  + [minus] is UnitKind Contract
  + [status] is Asserted
  + [named_expression] is exact bracketed name content after outer whitespace trim
  + [unnamed_expression] is exact body after outer whitespace trim
  + [meaning] is exact body after outer whitespace trim
  + [aliases] is empty
  + [context] is exact manifest scope, purpose, perspective, and world
  + [source_set] is stable document identity and source profile
  + [containment] is one Narrower relation from the syntactic parent to each syntactic child
  - never: resolve reference body text to an endpoint in this profile
  - never: infer alias, equivalence, causation, support, contradiction, permission, or authority from prose

& [StableIdentity] is digest-derived and collision-checked
  + [document_key] is lowercase project, namespace, and explicit document_id joined with length-delimited canonical encoding
  + [file_id] is file colon sop colon followed by lowercase first thirty-two hexadecimal SHA-256 digits of document_key
  + [node_key] is document_key, marker family, parent node key, normalized local name when present, and SHA-256 of normalized body
  + [normalization] is Unicode-preserving outer trim with ASCII case folding only
  + [unit_id] is unit colon sop colon followed by lowercase sixty-four hexadecimal SHA-256 digits of node_key
  + [clause_id] is clause colon sop colon followed by lowercase sixty-four hexadecimal SHA-256 digits of unit_id and source profile
  + [relation_id] is relation colon sop colon followed by lowercase sixty-four hexadecimal SHA-256 digits of Narrower plus endpoints
  + [relocation] is path and line number excluded from every semantic key
  + [duplicate] is any repeated document_key, node_key, file_id, unit_id, clause_id, or relation_id faults
  - never: append an encounter ordinal to repair identity collision

& [ParserFault] is deterministic inspectable failure
  + [kind] is InvalidManifest, Io, ResourceLimit, InvalidEncoding, InvalidSyntax, InvalidIndentation, DuplicateIdentity, Signing, Trust, ArtifactConflict, ArtifactWrite, or Verification
  + [document_id] is present for document faults
  + [path] is present when a file has been resolved
  + [line] is one-based when a line exists
  + [byte_start] is zero-based inclusive when a span exists
  + [byte_end] is zero-based exclusive when a span exists
  + [message] is deterministic and contains no source or private key bytes beyond a bounded escaped line preview
  + [ordering] is document manifest order then byte_start then kind
  = must: publish no environment when any parser or compilation fault exists

& [ResourceLimits] is bounded before allocation growth
  + [maximum_documents] is 256
  + [maximum_document_bytes] is 16777216
  + [maximum_corpus_bytes] is 67108864
  + [maximum_lines_per_document] is 200000
  + [maximum_nodes] is 1000000
  + [maximum_relations] is 1000000
  + [maximum_depth] is 128
  + [maximum_name_bytes] is 512
  + [maximum_body_bytes] is 65536
  + [maximum_query_templates] is 256

& [CorpusManifest] is strict portable configuration
  + [version] is cantor-sop-corpus/0.1
  + [source_root] is one relative directory resolved from the manifest directory
  + [document] is unique document_id and a relative path resolved beneath canonical source_root
  + [context] is nonempty project, namespace, scope, purpose, perspective, and world
  + [compiler] is valid SemanticId compiler_id, compiler_version, authority_signer_id, and compiler_signer_id
  + [trust] is nonempty dependency lock, proof identifiers, issue time, not-before time, and not-after time
  + [query_template] is a filesystem-safe unique name, nonempty term set, optional subject, and nonempty requested detail set
  + [unknown_fields] is rejected recursively
  + [source_root_escape] is allowed only because source_root itself is an explicit reviewed manifest field
  + [document_escape] is rejected after canonical resolution against source_root
  - never: include private key bytes or key file paths

& [OperatorCompiler] is the cantor-corpus binary
  + [command] is cantor-corpus compile
  + [required] is --manifest, --authority-key, --compiler-key, and --output
  + [optional] is --replace
  + [seed] is exactly thirty-two raw bytes or sixty-four ASCII hexadecimal digits plus zero or one final LF or CRLF
  + [separation] is signer identifiers differ and seed bytes differ
  + [preflight] is parse all documents, lower all units, detect all collisions, compile, construct trust store, admit package, construct requests, execute requests, and verify responses in memory
  + [output] is environment.json, inspect-fabric.json, query-NAME.json, and build-manifest.json
  + [publication] is same-directory temporary file, flush, close, and atomic rename for each absent or explicitly replaceable target
  + [receipt] is one JSON record containing profiles, public key fingerprints, package identity, certificate identity, environment digest, unit count, relation count, source count, artifact hashes, and timings
  + [replacement] is rejected unless --replace is explicit
  - never: emit, copy, hash into receipt, or persist private seed bytes

& [InitialSelfHostedCorpus] is tracked and reviewed
  + [manifest] is corpus\self_hosted\corpus.json
  + [source] is specifications\SOP_Core.sop
  + [source] is specifications\Cantor_Semantic_Coprocessor_Identity.sop
  + [source] is specifications\Cantor_Prepared_Runtime.sop
  + [query] is SemanticUnit requesting Term, Clause, SourceSpan, and Authority
  + [query] is Cantor requesting Term, Clause, SourceSpan, and Authority
  + [query] is PreparedRuntime requesting Term, Clause, SourceSpan, and Authority
  + [inspect] is fabric
  = must: compile every nonblank noncomment semantic line or reject the source

& [ArtifactAuthorityBoundary] is explicit
  + [tracked] is corpus manifest, source documents, schema contract, tests, benchmark method, and proof hashes
  + [generated_local] is key inputs, signed environment, requests, build receipt, and benchmark raw output
  + [ignore] is generated_local under .local
  + [rebuild] is mandatory after any selected source, manifest, compiler, dependency, validity, or key change
  + [runtime] is authorized only by recognized signatures, current TrustStore, exact environment digest, expected package set, requested scope, and proof verification
  - never: authorize a changed source through a previously generated package

